Z||000000||mbramble||05-23-2000||05:55 PM||||There was recently a thread on installing a CD player.  I did a search and found a link to it but it looks like it is gone??  Anyway, in it I mentioned that I had installed my CD changer and amp in the front of my car on a shelf mounted over the spare tire area.  Here are a couple of pics of the install for those of you who asked for them.  They can be viewed here:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.bramblett.com/fiero/stereo1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.bramblett.com/fiero/stereo1.jpg</A>  <BR>Cables have been left long until I can find some good plugs/connectors.  I hate these from Radio Shack and I don't think they will hold up well.  Amp is currently bypassed (simply plug the two cables coming from passenger are together instead of into/out of the amp -- I was thinking ahead!!) because of all the whine that showed up when I installed new front speakers that actually are able to reproduce sound!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.bramblett.com/fiero/stereo2.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.bramblett.com/fiero/stereo2.jpg</A> <BR>A view from the other side where you can see the bracket I mounted on the passenger side 'firewall' to support that end of the 3/4" plywood shelf.  A single wing nut holds the shelf to the support.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.bramblett.com/fiero/stereo3.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.bramblett.com/fiero/stereo3.jpg</A> <BR>A better view of the bracket.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.bramblett.com/fiero/stereo4.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.bramblett.com/fiero/stereo4.jpg</A> <BR>Support for the other end of the shelf comes from a 3/4" aluminum channel (shaped like  |_____|||4.4.102.203||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||05-24-2000||10:06 AM||||Looks nice, but I can see one problem.  At the back of the trunk there is a "holder" for the sunroof wind thing.  Also, you won't be able to set your sunroof under there when you remove it (can I assume you don't have a sunroof?).  I'll probably go with your idea but I'll have to modify it some and lower it a bit.  I plan to put my battery up front and remove the spare tire.  I just need to leave enough room for a couple of cans of Fix-A-Flat.  (I hate the stuff, but I need the space.)||||reg||1
